#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186682451 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f1d32e08-463e-50c2-92d4-d9e56827fb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{-5x-8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1d32e08-463e-50c2-92d4-d9e56827fb46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{-5x-8}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682453} :answer-field/id #uuid "88eb0ca2-ca71-506b-b692-99fa0d526b1d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186682449}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9e4f2970-f144-546f-8252-8a70c49b0c9c" :question/problem "Given that $y=\\sqrt{-5x-8}$, find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=-5x-8.$ Then $y=\\sqrt{u}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=-5.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{u}}\\cdot -5 \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{2\\sqrt{-5x-8}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186684216 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bb878bb6-46a7-5aeb-9186-804bc3feff65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{(3x-11)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684218}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bb878bb6-46a7-5aeb-9186-804bc3feff65" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{(3x-11)^{3}}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684218} :answer-field/id #uuid "9ab85c66-6a9d-57d1-87c6-3accb4436b41" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186684217}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3507e528-1e49-5249-b410-dabb462bd467" :question/problem "Find $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3x-11}}.$\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "We use the chain rule in the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nLet $u=3x-11.$ Then $y=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{u}}={u}^{-1/2}.$ Differentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}u}=-\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{-3/2}=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}},\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nMultiplying the two together gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{{u}^{3}}} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2\\sqrt{(3x-11)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c370c5b-a827-5030-99c8-35a1d2789f4a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i-2\\sin(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687391} {:answer/id #uuid "5b783484-c298-576c-b157-9ee1070a9501" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i+2\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687397} {:answer/id #uuid "751b2867-0c81-54d1-a87f-4f8ac4cfd769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i-2\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687399} {:answer/id #uuid "939b95c0-017f-52c0-91bd-e89a29989cbc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i-\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687404} {:answer/id #uuid "ac9a9237-d730-5e60-9e67-7bf268b7e8a4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i+\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687407}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "751b2867-0c81-54d1-a87f-4f8ac4cfd769" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i-2\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687399} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f8101f1-7c74-55a2-be80-25cba12fe050" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687402}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0f57d784-90da-542d-ba57-73dbd3c5607a" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y)=\\sin(x-2y)$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A function $f$ is a potential function for a vector field $\\mathbf F$ when $\\mathbf F=\\nabla f$. To identify the field, differentiate $f$ with respect to each coordinate, holding the other coordinates constant.\n\nThe chain rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x&=\\cos(x-2y)\\cdot 1=\\cos(x-2y),\\\\\nf_y&=\\cos(x-2y)\\cdot(-2)=-2\\cos(x-2y).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe factor $-2$ in $f_y$ comes from differentiating $x-2y$ with respect to $y$. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F=f_x\\,\\mathbf i+f_y\\,\\mathbf j=\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf i-2\\cos(x-2y)\\,\\mathbf j.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37990a22-b152-55cb-b3a8-1b7dabcf722c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(1+xz)e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+xy e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+(xy e^{xz}+2z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687394} {:answer/id #uuid "78680013-0452-588d-b0df-bb0c3581df44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(1+xz)e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+x e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+(x^2y e^{xz}+2z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687400} {:answer/id #uuid "a10abb11-e973-5675-843a-a85373052fc0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xyz e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+x e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+x^2y e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687405} {:answer/id #uuid "a5735a74-4e88-5a14-b53c-b038781896eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xyz e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+xy e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+(x^2y e^{xz}+2z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687406} {:answer/id #uuid "e549b683-6709-5b7f-b814-4b18d6e03605" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "xyz e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+x e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+(xy e^{xz}+2z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687409}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78680013-0452-588d-b0df-bb0c3581df44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y(1+xz)e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+x e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+(x^2y e^{xz}+2z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687400} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fd8a47a-c25d-5bfd-8924-c559e346714f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687403}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "16e58c58-212c-5d4a-859e-e8e997764d9d" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=xy e^{xz}+z^2$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A function $f$ is a potential function for a vector field $\\mathbf F$ when $\\mathbf F=\\nabla f$. To identify the field, differentiate $f$ with respect to each coordinate, holding the other coordinates constant.\n\nWhen differentiating with respect to $x$, both $xy$ and $e^{xz}$ depend on $x$, so we need the product rule as well as the chain rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x&=y e^{xz}+xy\\bigl(z e^{xz}\\bigr)\\\\\n   &=y(1+xz)e^{xz}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $f_y$, the exponential is constant with respect to $y$. For $f_z$, the factor $xy$ is constant, while both $e^{xz}$ and $z^2$ must be differentiated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_y&=x e^{xz},\\\\\nf_z&=xy\\bigl(x e^{xz}\\bigr)+2z=x^2y e^{xz}+2z.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the components in $x,y,z$ order gives\n\n$$\n\\mathbf F=\\nabla f=y(1+xz)e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf i+x e^{xz}\\,\\mathbf j+(x^2y e^{xz}+2z)\\,\\mathbf k.\n$$\n\nA candidate must agree in all three components. Omitting either term from the product rule, retaining an extra $y$ in $f_y$, or missing a term or chain-rule factor in $f_z$ changes the field."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687408 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b83f499-db08-5690-97e8-282559e6d9f4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j+\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687395} {:answer/id #uuid "5b3bbbbc-77b6-5088-9b12-e31d9c733e3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+x\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j+z\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687396} {:answer/id #uuid "633032a1-cca7-52f8-b513-bb392ee2645f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+x\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j-\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687398} {:answer/id #uuid "7da143d2-488d-52c0-88f1-543bc6417726" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+x\\sin(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j+\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687401} {:answer/id #uuid "fe2a71d0-65dd-5016-8cc4-986ad1118668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+x\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j+\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe2a71d0-65dd-5016-8cc4-986ad1118668" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+x\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j+\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687411} :answer-field/id #uuid "f45feee5-9a3a-522a-9a6f-7b337ab06128" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687410}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ad88db5c-9649-5e6c-b098-3ba7d8c62108" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=\\sin(xy+z)$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A function $f$ is a potential function for a vector field $\\mathbf F$ when $\\mathbf F=\\nabla f$. To identify the field, differentiate $f$ with respect to each coordinate, holding the other coordinates constant.\n\nThere are three components. The inner function $xy+z$ has partial derivatives $y$, $x$, and $1$, respectively. Applying the chain rule,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf_x&=y\\cos(xy+z),\\\\\nf_y&=x\\cos(xy+z),\\\\\nf_z&=\\cos(xy+z).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIn particular, differentiating with respect to $z$ contributes a factor of $1$, not $z$. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\mathbf F=\\nabla f&=y\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf i+x\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf j\\\\&\\quad+\\cos(xy+z)\\,\\mathbf k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687810 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e319542-3e6b-5d94-8091-3f053a0a5635" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12 x\\,i+24 y\\,j-4 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687803} {:answer/id #uuid "50614548-764f-5d72-950a-fc60a66c7aaf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18 x\\,i+0\\,j-4 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687804} {:answer/id #uuid "907e0aea-1a07-5731-80c3-4b7b1a5c24f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 x\\,i+8 y\\,j-8 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687807} {:answer/id #uuid "b5327e59-6585-5c3b-896c-2884a9550fc3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-12 x\\,i+24 y\\,j-16 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687809} {:answer/id #uuid "d476c136-1223-595c-bfa3-77e575339294" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-18 x\\,i+4 y\\,j-24 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687812}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "907e0aea-1a07-5731-80c3-4b7b1a5c24f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6 x\\,i+8 y\\,j-8 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687807} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc7dd5df-5712-5b1f-bb92-c19426fdf116" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687813}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b85a3cfe-7298-5470-a204-b727115cf9a1" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=- 3 x^{2} + 4 y^{2} - 4 z^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=\\nabla f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f &=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,i+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,j+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,k \\\\ &=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- 3 x^{2} + 4 y^{2} - 4 z^{2}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad +\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 3 x^{2} + 4 y^{2} - 4 z^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad +\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}\\left(- 3 x^{2} + 4 y^{2} - 4 z^{2}\\right)\\,k \\\\ &=-6 x\\,i+8 y\\,j-8 z\\,k \\\\ &=F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=-6 x\\,i+8 y\\,j-8 z\\,k.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687811 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec14d19-8a78-5735-af04-7f05723b09d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24 x y z\\,i+0\\,j-12 z\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687801} {:answer/id #uuid "292cb243-c779-57be-b854-306331487ea6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0\\,i-8 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(8 z+4 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687802} {:answer/id #uuid "6305d519-17e8-5017-a5be-7488154d58ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-24 x y z\\,i-2 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(4 z+4 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687805} {:answer/id #uuid "979b8a0c-5739-536f-8650-954b62ec870a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8 x y z\\,i-4 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(4 z+4 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687808} {:answer/id #uuid "f9df8eda-fd1b-5796-a963-5cd5dfa146a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8 x y z\\,i-2 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(8 z+12 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687814}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "979b8a0c-5739-536f-8650-954b62ec870a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8 x y z\\,i-4 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(4 z+4 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687808} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f8c9cbd-3c6a-5454-baf3-abc9a81fb962" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687806}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "cac6e87e-9791-5b22-ada7-5a75166a3c33" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=- 4 x^{2} y z - 2 z^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A vector field $F$ is conservative if it is the gradient of a scalar function $f.$ That is, there exists a function $f$ such that $F=\\nabla f.$ The function $f$ is called a potential function for $F.$\n\nTo compute the vector field associated with a potential function $f,$ we compute its gradient:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\nabla f &=\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial x}\\,i+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial y}\\,j+\\frac{\\partial f}{\\partial z}\\,k \\\\ &=\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial x}\\left(- 4 x^{2} y z - 2 z^{2}\\right)\\,i \\\\ &\\quad +\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial y}\\left(- 4 x^{2} y z - 2 z^{2}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &\\quad +\\frac{\\partial}{\\partial z}\\left(- 4 x^{2} y z - 2 z^{2}\\right)\\,k \\\\ &=-8 x y z\\,i-4 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(4 z+4 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k \\\\ &=F\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector field that has $f$ as a potential function is\n\n$$\nF=-8 x y z\\,i-4 x^{2} z\\,j-\\left(4 z+4 x^{2} y\\right)\\,k.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687828 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171e8a20-ab06-51cf-b37c-2b9f6bb81251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-6 y e^{- x z}+6 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-2 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(2 z+2 x^{2} y e^{- x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687817} {:answer/id #uuid "38c24c9f-02f4-59e7-a22b-edafe89564bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-4 y e^{- x z}+4 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-2 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(8 z+2 x^{2} y e^{- x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687819} {:answer/id #uuid "5b9bbd1b-80f2-5df0-a448-9c244862d8dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-1 y e^{- x z}+1 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-4 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(2 z+6 x^{2} y e^{- x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687822} {:answer/id #uuid "66703a61-730d-50f6-a952-39ac2648db64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-1 y e^{- x z}+6 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-1 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+12 z\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687823} {:answer/id #uuid "9e59f109-3dc3-50c7-9a33-c5824878e3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-2 y e^{- x z}+2 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-2 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{- x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687831}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9e59f109-3dc3-50c7-9a33-c5824878e3d8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-2 y e^{- x z}+2 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-2 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{- x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687831} :answer-field/id #uuid "685dac0f-5b77-5258-abde-52b7e9e2ed7b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687824}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8ad9fdce-7a7a-5333-8440-46f69e86db18" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y e^{- x z} + 2 z^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A potential function satisfies $F=\\nabla f$. Differentiate with respect to each coordinate, holding the others constant.\n\nFor $f_x$, both factors of $- 2 x y e^{- x z}$ depend on $x$, so the product and chain rules give\n\n$$\nf_x=- 2 ye^{- x z}+(- 2 x y)(- z)e^{- x z}.\n$$\n\nFor $f_y$, the exponential is constant. For $f_z$, apply the chain rule to the exponential and differentiate the added quadratic. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x&=2 x y z e^{- x z} - 2 y e^{- x z} \\\\ f_y&=- 2 x e^{- x z} \\\\ f_z&=2 x^{2} y e^{- x z} + 4 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the components in $x,y,z$ order,\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(-2 y e^{- x z}+2 x y z e^{- x z}\\right)\\,i-2 x e^{- x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{- x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687833 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a214ba9-8025-55ff-ae3d-ef1f01724fce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(0.5 y e^{2 x z}+4 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+0.5 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+6 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687821} {:answer/id #uuid "915cfdca-5a2e-5db1-8212-3fb9914e9ca7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(1 y e^{2 x z}+4 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+0.5 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-8 z+1 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687829} {:answer/id #uuid "b90bfec9-8ce9-53ff-b511-25e7f412b1df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 y e^{2 x z}+1 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+1 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+1 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687835} {:answer/id #uuid "f7e675c7-68c3-5076-988f-9b841c93b1be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(1 y e^{2 x z}+2 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+1 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687841} {:answer/id #uuid "f9870986-7d12-557e-9ccf-04377f6435ac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(0.5 y e^{2 x z}+1 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+2 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-2 z+1 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687843}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7e675c7-68c3-5076-988f-9b841c93b1be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(1 y e^{2 x z}+2 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+1 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687841} :answer-field/id #uuid "854c9274-8345-5ab3-b4fc-3f21132d4275" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687827}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a837792b-8839-5f6b-8203-352f9c43c6a5" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=x y e^{2 x z} - 2 z^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A potential function satisfies $F=\\nabla f$. Differentiate with respect to each coordinate, holding the others constant.\n\nFor $f_x$, both factors of $x y e^{2 x z}$ depend on $x$, so the product and chain rules give\n\n$$\nf_x=ye^{2 x z}+(x y)(2 z)e^{2 x z}.\n$$\n\nFor $f_y$, the exponential is constant. For $f_z$, apply the chain rule to the exponential and differentiate the added quadratic. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x&=2 x y z e^{2 x z} + y e^{2 x z} \\\\ f_y&=x e^{2 x z} \\\\ f_z&=2 x^{2} y e^{2 x z} - 4 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the components in $x,y,z$ order,\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(1 y e^{2 x z}+2 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+1 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687834 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2efd5ed5-0b3a-59b4-a307-3c41181bda93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 y e^{2 x z}+4 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+2 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+4 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687818} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd1cfc8-ddf5-5dd5-838a-ea12728b65b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 y e^{2 x z}+2 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+4 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+2 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687826} {:answer/id #uuid "ce4112da-ace7-5f37-bf80-fd8e9d0c0708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(6 y e^{2 x z}+2 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+4 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-12 z+12 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687837} {:answer/id #uuid "d96c4904-c039-5e83-a2ee-5541458b0d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(6 y e^{2 x z}+4 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+6 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &-12 z\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687838} {:answer/id #uuid "f970242a-3d9a-521a-8ba1-7cb0bcb6fb6b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&6 y e^{2 x z}\\,i+1 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &-2 z\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687842}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2efd5ed5-0b3a-59b4-a307-3c41181bda93" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 y e^{2 x z}+4 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+2 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+4 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687818} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ad6858f-3175-5a2d-a3e7-12e9f2b99164" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687820}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ab21f9f2-ed86-500e-8ce0-d220b095f7f0" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=2 x y e^{2 x z} - 2 z^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A potential function satisfies $F=\\nabla f$. Differentiate with respect to each coordinate, holding the others constant.\n\nFor $f_x$, both factors of $2 x y e^{2 x z}$ depend on $x$, so the product and chain rules give\n\n$$\nf_x=2 ye^{2 x z}+(2 x y)(2 z)e^{2 x z}.\n$$\n\nFor $f_y$, the exponential is constant. For $f_z$, apply the chain rule to the exponential and differentiate the added quadratic. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x&=4 x y z e^{2 x z} + 2 y e^{2 x z} \\\\ f_y&=2 x e^{2 x z} \\\\ f_z&=4 x^{2} y e^{2 x z} - 4 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the components in $x,y,z$ order,\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{aligned}&\\left(2 y e^{2 x z}+4 x y z e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,i+2 x e^{2 x z}\\,j \\\\ &+\\left(-4 z+4 x^{2} y e^{2 x z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186687836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06a69543-4b8c-5e81-b77f-51eac74e6361" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&-1 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-\\left(6 x e^{2 y z}+8 x y z e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(12 z+12 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687816} {:answer/id #uuid "931f797a-cbda-5c73-b2bc-946a793c1c54" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&-2 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-\\left(4 x e^{2 y z}+2 x y z e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(12 z+8 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687830} {:answer/id #uuid "a25a72ed-2fbd-5a85-9e8b-c57eb1a27a71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&-6 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-\\left(4 x e^{2 y z}+8 x y z e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(2 z+12 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687832} {:answer/id #uuid "e5358a34-96e5-5884-bae0-ffaf392318b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&-2 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-\\left(2 x e^{2 y z}+4 x y z e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(4 z+4 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687839} {:answer/id #uuid "ee3324d6-a8f5-5481-a556-079d6485c20f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&-2 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-2 x y z e^{2 y z}\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(8 z+12 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687840}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e5358a34-96e5-5884-bae0-ffaf392318b3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{aligned}&-2 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-\\left(2 x e^{2 y z}+4 x y z e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(4 z+4 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687839} :answer-field/id #uuid "72bfb587-ba18-5fff-92ed-22afc1f10c1e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186687825}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c2173467-b4b2-5231-ab56-5e9bb4621557" :question/problem "For which of the following vector fields is $f(x,y,z)=- 2 x y e^{2 y z} - 2 z^{2}$ a potential function?" :question/worked-solution "A potential function satisfies $F=\\nabla f$. Differentiate with respect to each coordinate, holding the others constant.\n\nFor $f_y$, both factors of $- 2 x y e^{2 y z}$ depend on $y$, so the product and chain rules give\n\n$$\nf_y=- 2 xe^{2 y z}+(- 2 x y)(2 z)e^{2 y z}.\n$$\n\nFor $f_x$, the exponential is constant. For $f_z$, apply the chain rule to the exponential and differentiate the added quadratic. Thus,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f_x&=- 2 y e^{2 y z} \\\\ f_y&=- 4 x y z e^{2 y z} - 2 x e^{2 y z} \\\\ f_z&=- 4 x y^{2} e^{2 y z} - 4 z\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nPutting the components in $x,y,z$ order,\n\n$$\nF=\\begin{aligned}&-2 y e^{2 y z}\\,i-\\left(2 x e^{2 y z}+4 x y z e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,j \\\\ &-\\left(4 z+4 x y^{2} e^{2 y z}\\right)\\,k\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696533 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ea8bd68-1a74-5249-8f8d-463b0a21b3d3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos^2{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696532} {:answer/id #uuid "574d6a25-a683-5956-9070-15fdf2a941b2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696536} {:answer/id #uuid "5a1cbffb-7df3-5b5c-aeb7-235cc062d829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696537} {:answer/id #uuid "6e839309-bec5-5e57-8705-a92245ef235f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696540} {:answer/id #uuid "d6df07c3-84bb-57f9-80c1-cb388447ccc6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a1cbffb-7df3-5b5c-aeb7-235cc062d829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696537} :answer-field/id #uuid "96315e4c-fe80-5791-a296-0690184975c6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696545}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "34945772-932c-5b8e-8cb1-67dfefb2fc5e" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression\n\n$$\n2\\cos^3{x}+2\\cos{x}\\sin^2{x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Factor the common factor $2\\cos{x}$ from both terms:\n\n$$\n2\\cos^3{x}+2\\cos{x}\\sin^2{x}\n=2\\cos{x}(\\cos^2{x}+\\sin^2{x}).\n$$\n\nThe Pythagorean identity gives $\\cos^2{x}+\\sin^2{x}=1$, so\n\n$$\n2\\cos{x}(\\cos^2{x}+\\sin^2{x})=2\\cos{x}\\cdot 1=2\\cos{x}.\n$$\n\nThe simplified expression is $2\\cos{x}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696534 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7a10277c-5350-5a72-b15b-edea90628e39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696541} {:answer/id #uuid "82692cf9-89d7-552b-b7d3-1ac691efea46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696543} {:answer/id #uuid "e77cf5d8-bd0c-5975-97df-3a1e5b557316" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin^2{x}-\\cos^2{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696550} {:answer/id #uuid "ea6ab931-7d8d-58df-974f-e5bcedca8ee1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin^2{x}+\\sin{x}\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696551} {:answer/id #uuid "fe446486-8476-542a-89c8-c15d257b7993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin^2{x}-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696552}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe446486-8476-542a-89c8-c15d257b7993" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin^2{x}-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696552} :answer-field/id #uuid "8a0fd7b4-dbe3-59d5-a172-d844e41a9be2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696544}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "37d59388-6581-560b-b7a1-31ef074d1897" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression\n\n$$\n\\sin^4{x}-\\sin{x}\\cos^3{x}+\\sin^2{x}\\cos^2{x}-\\sin^3{x}\\cos{x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Group the two positive terms and the two negative terms. This makes two different common factors available:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(\\sin^4{x}+\\sin^2{x}\\cos^2{x})\\\\\n&\\qquad-(\\sin{x}\\cos^3{x}+\\sin^3{x}\\cos{x}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFactor $\\sin^2{x}$ from the first group and $\\sin{x}\\cos{x}$ from the group being subtracted:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\sin^2{x}(\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x})\\\\\n&\\qquad-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}(\\cos^2{x}+\\sin^2{x}).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEach parenthesized sum equals $1$ by the Pythagorean identity. The minus sign applies to the whole second group:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin^2{x}\\cdot 1-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}\\cdot 1\n&=\\sin^2{x}-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe simplified expression is $\\sin^2{x}-\\sin{x}\\cos{x}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186696546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6505f6c5-42ae-5140-b464-c125bb0dc0f7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{x}+\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696538} {:answer/id #uuid "6b7d6706-2cd5-5d1e-9529-851cecb61805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696539} {:answer/id #uuid "7c7d2ef0-79c7-5a95-af84-62b0fbf94be6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696542} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8bfeaa-eb8e-58a8-bb69-bc6cdff5a57c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696547} {:answer/id #uuid "d1a9bba7-6280-5751-a9b2-55d3cb24f84e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696548}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b7d6706-2cd5-5d1e-9529-851cecb61805" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696539} :answer-field/id #uuid "470d29d3-ad8b-5109-8bb4-bea361adf806" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186696535}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b26797c7-4ed6-51e5-aa94-fad3f09c0d8d" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression\n\n$$\n\\sin^3{x}-\\cos{x}+\\sin{x}\\cos^2{x}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "The first and third terms have a common factor $\\sin{x}$. Group them, keeping the middle term negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&(\\sin^3{x}+\\sin{x}\\cos^2{x})-\\cos{x}\\\\\n&=\\sin{x}(\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x})-\\cos{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse $\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x}=1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\sin{x}(\\sin^2{x}+\\cos^2{x})-\\cos{x}\\\\\n&=\\sin{x}\\cdot 1-\\cos{x}\\\\\n&=\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe simplified expression is $\\sin{x}-\\cos{x}$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697056 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02399fbc-6085-5417-bd08-b413d7bc0b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697055} {:answer/id #uuid "10ee8e14-324c-5d5f-b65f-67854a40d4ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\cos{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697060} {:answer/id #uuid "509f26c1-fafd-5495-af7a-2fcabee31f94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\cos{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697064} {:answer/id #uuid "8bd361b0-662c-5d1a-8382-f3cd8ba7803f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697072} {:answer/id #uuid "9ce2ea25-a127-52de-aaf2-ab8e290d9352" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697074}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02399fbc-6085-5417-bd08-b413d7bc0b40" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sin{\\alpha}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697055} :answer-field/id #uuid "e881b892-e286-59b4-8561-db3ca720ad08" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697085}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "04bddd12-0613-5cb0-bf6e-263792e636c4" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}+2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}+2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha} \\\\ &=2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\alpha}+\\cos^{2}{\\alpha}) \\\\ &=2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=2\\sin{\\alpha}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&2\\sin^{3}{\\alpha}+2\\sin{\\alpha}\\cos^{2}{\\alpha} \\\\ &=2\\sin{\\alpha}\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697078 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "070cb534-4f96-5379-b409-3ec04458fb83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697057} {:answer/id #uuid "0cdbe935-e409-5229-a790-bf0046a6ad41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697059} {:answer/id #uuid "28693c90-2019-5ea7-8d8c-6cd9564afb39" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697062} {:answer/id #uuid "74e7171d-4ed0-5fd1-98a6-2c89288b37b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697069} {:answer/id #uuid "ea0deefb-437d-5d42-8b22-17dcce306882" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697086}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "74e7171d-4ed0-5fd1-98a6-2c89288b37b4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697069} :answer-field/id #uuid "a76ae156-a250-51fb-a3e1-24a516771871" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697077}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b27325c7-4b05-5192-850e-374baf7b8a18" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-4\\sin^{3}{x}-4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-4\\sin^{3}{x}-4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x} \\\\ &=-4\\sin{x}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-4\\sin{x}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}) \\\\ &=-4\\sin{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=-4\\sin{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-4\\sin^{3}{x}-4\\sin{x}\\cos^{2}{x} \\\\ &=-4\\sin{x}\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697079 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fd2796a-8d94-5f09-9b82-77d3ae757ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697073} {:answer/id #uuid "a08d04ab-422a-5199-b4a9-a687a5257eb9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697075} {:answer/id #uuid "a3187c31-4d89-56df-8198-848feb388b03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697076} {:answer/id #uuid "fdf2061c-a9e4-5819-a1e4-14eaf76e9961" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697087} {:answer/id #uuid "ff7f6014-ceda-50d8-b386-9b4f73936467" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sin{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697089}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fd2796a-8d94-5f09-9b82-77d3ae757ebf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\cos{x}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697073} :answer-field/id #uuid "7078f67a-b10c-5e41-9baa-dd14cdcbf0c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697067}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "bf324e6f-a2d1-5c0d-8f69-cc3efc8ed63d" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-3\\sin^{2}{x}\\cos{x}-3\\cos^{3}{x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-3\\sin^{2}{x}\\cos{x}-3\\cos^{3}{x} \\\\ &=-3\\cos{x}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-3\\cos{x}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{x}+\\cos^{2}{x}) \\\\ &=-3\\cos{x}\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=-3\\cos{x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-3\\sin^{2}{x}\\cos{x}-3\\cos^{3}{x} \\\\ &=-3\\cos{x}\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697081 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49dbec6d-159c-58b8-8e26-479f98c952db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697063} {:answer/id #uuid "7b6a8712-dc68-5e87-bd8f-af0e4e9fbec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697070} {:answer/id #uuid "8371ea1c-3f45-599f-b7dc-60df4510d031" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697071} {:answer/id #uuid "d0111010-8a7c-56a4-9ca7-610f719be677" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697082} {:answer/id #uuid "fe4ccd2a-2375-5e1d-8608-8b19768377e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697088}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4ccd2a-2375-5e1d-8608-8b19768377e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697088} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e81c75d-fee7-5338-b39f-00f66dff51f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697061}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf0282c7-e92b-537b-88cf-fb240a021222" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $5\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}+5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&5\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}+5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta} \\\\ &=5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}) \\\\ &=5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&5\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}+5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos^{3}{\\theta} \\\\ &=5\\sin{\\theta}\\cos{\\theta}\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697083 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c930511-ee2a-530d-8ba4-710444598a5f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697058} {:answer/id #uuid "55a32a20-1571-51b8-99a9-b5d9e7f2ce00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5\\sin^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697065} {:answer/id #uuid "5c5616ba-da50-5ba2-86f3-b71806cf1fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697066} {:answer/id #uuid "70a448b0-7260-5b63-8f6e-7e51b4c9a972" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697068} {:answer/id #uuid "dc4545dc-851e-5283-adb0-8412976ae897" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4\\cos^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697084}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5c5616ba-da50-5ba2-86f3-b71806cf1fa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697066} :answer-field/id #uuid "c79ae8bc-35c7-545e-803f-eeb27731b734" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697080}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d846fc03-0075-52e3-9b26-7527092af06f" :question/problem "Simplify the trigonometric expression $-\\sin^{5}{\\theta}-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we factor the expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-\\sin^{5}{\\theta}-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta} \\\\ &=-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use $\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}=1$ to simplify the expression in the parentheses:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot(\\sin^{2}{\\theta}+\\cos^{2}{\\theta}) \\\\ &=-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cdot 1 \\\\ &=-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&-\\sin^{5}{\\theta}-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\cos^{2}{\\theta} \\\\ &=-\\sin^{3}{\\theta}\\end{aligned}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697156 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6299f072-9ed7-5551-a10c-63ca9a9e0a0f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(2x)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697159} {:answer/id #uuid "8c317928-bbbb-5b46-a97f-38516707afa9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697160} {:answer/id #uuid "8d8d0e3e-86ba-5ca8-a071-4abe73324087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(2x+1)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697161} {:answer/id #uuid "b55753b5-2d5f-5e5e-8179-950befc2864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697164} {:answer/id #uuid "ebaa5507-673b-5495-9c4e-f5a9d3758829" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697168}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b55753b5-2d5f-5e5e-8179-950befc2864c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6(2x+1)^2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697164} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcb1b353-f6ca-5091-82a4-46c3c308f2e7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "16ea0705-2342-5b78-944f-84d5268fd2eb" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(2x+1)^3$, find $f'(x)$.\n\nUse the decomposition $g(x)=2x+1$ and $F(u)=u^3$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$. Recall that $f'(x)=F'(g(x))g'(x)$." :question/worked-solution "Differentiate the outer and inner functions separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF'(u)&=3u^2, \\\\\ng'(x)&=2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule multiplies the outer derivative, evaluated at the unchanged inner expression, by the inner derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=F'(g(x))g'(x) \\\\\n&=3(2x+1)^2\\cdot 2 \\\\\n&=6(2x+1)^2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697162 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e61cb88-4009-5620-84fc-a9080a4da648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697157}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e61cb88-4009-5620-84fc-a9080a4da648" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-2x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697157} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c66ad95-0e1a-5f4f-b282-666f579aebe1" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697158}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9bc757c8-8f4c-5efa-890c-24f6558197c9" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\dfrac{2}{\\sqrt{x^2-3x+3}}$, complete the expression for $f'(x)$ by entering the missing factor.\n\n$f'(x)=\\dfrac{1}{(x^2-3x+3)^{3/2}}\\,($ {{field-1}} $)$" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=x^2-3x+3$ and rewrite the outer function as $F(u)=2u^{-1/2}$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiate the outer and inner functions:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF'(u)&=2\\left(-\\frac12\\right)u^{-3/2}=-u^{-3/2}, \\\\\ng'(x)&=2x-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the chain rule gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=F'(g(x))g'(x) \\\\\n&=-(x^2-3x+3)^{-3/2}(2x-3) \\\\\n&=\\frac{3-2x}{(x^2-3x+3)^{3/2}} \\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{(x^2-3x+3)^{3/2}}(3-2x).\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe missing factor is $3-2x$. It includes both the inner derivative and the outer derivative's factor of $-1$.\n\nSince $x^2-3x+3=(x-\\frac32)^2+\\frac34>0$, this derivative is defined for every real $x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697163 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bd39cb58-6343-57f1-aaba-008b64577b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8(3-2x)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd39cb58-6343-57f1-aaba-008b64577b84" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8(3-2x)^3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697165} :answer-field/id #uuid "c3f18178-7a19-5ada-8f9e-6db3f7e933b2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697166}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "b2e6e7b9-4715-540f-bb2f-b216b11323a6" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(3-2x)^4$, find $f'(x)$.\n\n$f'(x)=$ {{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let $g(x)=3-2x$ and $F(u)=u^4$, so $f(x)=F(g(x))$.\n\nDifferentiate each function:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nF'(u)&=4u^3, \\\\\ng'(x)&=-2.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApply the chain rule and substitute $g(x)=3-2x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf'(x)&=F'(g(x))g'(x) \\\\\n&=4(3-2x)^3\\cdot(-2) \\\\\n&=-8(3-2x)^3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe inner derivative supplies the negative sign; the inner expression itself stays $3-2x$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697642 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1ac25246-3153-5bc7-9c7a-e1323ff4efcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1ac25246-3153-5bc7-9c7a-e1323ff4efcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697637} :answer-field/id #uuid "29dd3737-7889-5d0d-aee8-9285c4931e86" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697638} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c79a8f1f-cb00-506d-bd4b-a3fb8ef0e424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697650}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c79a8f1f-cb00-506d-bd4b-a3fb8ef0e424" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697650} :answer-field/id #uuid "6b9ac73b-7b7d-5e34-bbe8-45b0c4d75776" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697643} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ac8f7f0-05b6-55ff-a51f-14433d0c00a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697648}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9ac8f7f0-05b6-55ff-a51f-14433d0c00a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697648} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5a1377a-b174-5967-b4e3-0492fec907ed" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697652}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "68ea139d-8f83-5ecb-b070-c337ebdf0983" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=2t-1,\\qquad y=t^2+1,\\qquad -2\\le t\\le 2.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks. Use the value of $t$ at the top of each column in the formula for that row. For example, the first entry in the $x$-row is $x(-2)=2(-2)-1=-5$.\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-5$ | {{field-1}} | $-1$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |\n| $y$ | {{field-3}} | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ |" :question/worked-solution "The row tells us which formula to use, and the column tells us the value of $t$.\n\nFor the $x$-entry under $t=-1$, substitute $-1$ into $x=2t-1$:\n\n$$\nx(-1)=2(-1)-1=-2-1=-3.\n$$\n\nFor the $x$-entry under $t=2$, use the same formula:\n\n$$\nx(2)=2(2)-1=4-1=3.\n$$\n\nFor the $y$-entry under $t=-2$, use $y=t^2+1$. Square the entire negative number:\n\n$$\ny(-2)=(-2)^2+1=4+1=5.\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-5$ | $-3$ | $-1$ | $1$ | $3$ |\n| $y$ | $5$ | $2$ | $1$ | $2$ | $5$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697645 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0aa20801-08a2-5e2d-950e-e3cc94ff6da5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-2}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697633} {:answer/id #uuid "33dd7ec4-0126-5adf-812f-11166227af2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697639} {:answer/id #uuid "4612bcf9-ddbe-577d-8ecf-f5c64ae4b720" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697640} {:answer/id #uuid "620e6851-0bd2-5bf8-b300-14d8ebc4ddda" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697641} {:answer/id #uuid "8fe19e41-701e-5fe0-b25b-dd12d35b61a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}+1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697647}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "33dd7ec4-0126-5adf-812f-11166227af2c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697639} :answer-field/id #uuid "b429b33e-f0af-50a0-b280-3a1a49ca466d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "86dd7dd4-5849-554c-9e2d-91445aacb13c" :question/problem "For the parametric curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{4}\\right),\\qquad y=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi t}{6}\\right),\\qquad -3\\le t\\le 4,\n$$\n\nconsider the following table of values. Angles are in radians.\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $a$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $b$ | $1$ | $c$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |\n\nFind the exact value of $a-b+c$." :question/worked-solution "Read each letter's row and column before substituting.\n\nThe entry $a$ is an $x$-value at $t=-3$:\n\n$$\na=\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi(-3)}{4}\\right)=\\sin\\left(-\\frac{3\\pi}{4}\\right)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nHere $\\sin(-\\theta)=-\\sin\\theta$ and $\\sin(3\\pi/4)=\\sqrt{2}/2$.\n\nThe entry $b$ is a $y$-value at $t=-2$:\n\n$$\nb=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(-2)}{6}\\right)=\\cos\\left(-\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\right)=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nCosine is even, so $\\cos(-\\pi/3)=\\cos(\\pi/3)$.\n\nThe entry $c$ is a $y$-value at $t=1$:\n\n$$\nc=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi(1)}{6}\\right)=\\cos\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{6}\\right)=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, substitute these three entries into the requested expression, keeping the subtraction before $b$:\n\n$$\na-b+c=-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-\\sqrt{2}-1}{2}.\n$$\n\nThe completed table is\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $0$ | $1$ | $4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $1$ | $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ | $-\\frac{1}{2}$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697653 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3f6cd6f-feb8-5fe8-8a90-33632f5509a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697651}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3f6cd6f-feb8-5fe8-8a90-33632f5509a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697651} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d405c02-fc58-51d3-b300-ae1c90f40fc4" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697634} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1160877a-343d-5fc8-aac7-64b1af59bba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697635}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1160877a-343d-5fc8-aac7-64b1af59bba7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697635} :answer-field/id #uuid "12a46afb-ed30-514f-a742-c43b99568561" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697636} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8bcf4e3f-6edb-5253-90d7-a2b123cbc029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697646}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8bcf4e3f-6edb-5253-90d7-a2b123cbc029" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697646} :answer-field/id #uuid "80b84a21-8b7e-5c23-91e4-90c00658f335" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697644}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fca75a6f-ed74-5c52-b7db-81a5147488d0" :question/problem "Consider the curve with parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=t^2-t,\\qquad y=\\frac{t+1}{t-1},\\qquad -3\\le t\\le 0.\n$$\n\nFill in the three blanks in the table. Give exact values.\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $12$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | {{field-2}} | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $0$ | {{field-3}} |" :question/worked-solution "The missing $x$-entry is in the column $t=-2$. Substitute into $x=t^2-t$:\n\n$$\nx(-2)=(-2)^2-(-2)=4+2=6.\n$$\n\nFor the missing $y$-entries, substitute the column's parameter into both the numerator and the denominator of $y=\\frac{t+1}{t-1}$:\n\n$$\ny(-3)=\\frac{-3+1}{-3-1}=\\frac{-2}{-4}=\\frac{1}{2},\n$$\n\n$$\ny(0)=\\frac{0+1}{0-1}=\\frac{1}{-1}=-1.\n$$\n\nThe denominators are nonzero at all the listed parameter values. The completed table is\n\n| $t$ | $-3$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $12$ | $6$ | $2$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $\\frac{1}{2}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $0$ | $-1$ |"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6ec46b73-c5f6-5155-959c-ca6e0c3d1663" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/60/60a8e096bb5a75c2b9d719cb7e8cae14fb27bc9d8e4b33455bc562c731382d9e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697895} {:answer/id #uuid "865b8979-1018-585a-94ed-051c773c0096" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/12/12ced3191f8d54a6d579de66db1a0f291de774a6365f0a047269b2d822b67223.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697899} {:answer/id #uuid "92bce595-3de9-5315-a86a-f69867d20547" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/1b/1b6df959601589325952b589fdd198e5655b827a0fade7d27968e8295855ff6b.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697900} {:answer/id #uuid "c772bb43-715e-5648-baeb-0e6e47a14099" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/0e/0e57de3a6543dce1df686135dc40e855e7487f5eb15f48aa63da28bcd5cdb094.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697904} {:answer/id #uuid "dd5aa83a-8c1f-58c1-b2c8-ee3307ba8194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d70fcd150196f121250a2f3bf1460adb87e4f91e51f838807814de9edcff54e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697906}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dd5aa83a-8c1f-58c1-b2c8-ee3307ba8194" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/4d/4d70fcd150196f121250a2f3bf1460adb87e4f91e51f838807814de9edcff54e.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697906} :answer-field/id #uuid "d0f6b3cb-b6b7-5010-be72-77857f2bad2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697905}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3bd93405-82bc-5458-ab8c-fc0a7f96a9e3" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t(t-2),\\qquad y=t(t+2),\\qquad -2\\leq t\\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Create a table of paired coordinates. First calculate the $x$-values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $8$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow calculate the $y$-values at the same parameter values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $8$ | $3$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ |\n| $y$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ | $8$ |\n\nThe successive points are $(8,0)$, $(3,-1)$, $(0,0)$, $(-1,3)$ and $(0,8)$. Both coordinates turn within the interval: $x=(t-1)^2-1$ has minimum $-1$ at $t=1$, while $y=(t+1)^2-1$ has minimum $-1$ at $t=-1$. Plot a smooth curve through the paired points in parameter order. It dips below the $x$-axis through $(3,-1)$, passes through the origin, then bends left of the $y$-axis through $(-1,3)$ before reaching $(0,8)$. All five choices share the endpoints and the origin, so those three checkpoints alone cannot decide the answer. Check both interior bends.\n\n![The curve through the calculated points](images/86/8644be497d26e662b3b867539ee7b8d0dd812fac915e55db7b05045592a4fc6e.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "171dba7b-75a8-5827-b2b7-f3f105018aa4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f0/f07139da8afc6442b5d9281b35a6fd87c1cbcd3cd1e5a692afd45cf7a06e5a1a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697889} {:answer/id #uuid "1b08777a-5263-568c-8e9a-927145630fc1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/78/783773aee472c70476a015a44fb648a8e59ac81bb8b564e2de6fede2a3c7cec8.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697890} {:answer/id #uuid "3a872233-4f07-505d-b731-f999cd3d4b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/331b287274e591bba469912c94bb7a7b6901dc929184d9c352ce88d8ca89a4ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697892} {:answer/id #uuid "f237f7bb-1ab1-5d28-8739-08cf56324c00" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dc/dca67dd9991b9a24320fcc8527020926b9c14400f82c26d86657d4f76fc6436f.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697907} {:answer/id #uuid "f77a222c-1429-5aa3-ba95-e1aa7abf488b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/7b/7bb54e148382c9b93b3669893a0f9672dcd442acd6db2ebed4c5b5a3c8ac42f5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a872233-4f07-505d-b731-f999cd3d4b52" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/33/331b287274e591bba469912c94bb7a7b6901dc929184d9c352ce88d8ca89a4ee.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697892} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e236298-acd4-58ed-84ad-c655d28e371f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697888}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "596432d1-4b77-548d-b59e-39a7ad303e6d" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t+2,\\qquad y=1-t,\\qquad -2\\leq t\\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Create a table of paired coordinates. First calculate the $x$-values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow calculate the $y$-values at the same parameter values:\n\n| $t$ | $-2$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ | $-1$ |\n\nThe paired coordinates are $(0,3)$, $(1,2)$, $(2,1)$, $(3,0)$ and $(4,-1)$. They lie on a decreasing straight line. Keep only the segment from $(0,3)$ to $(4,-1)$, with both endpoints included. A line with the right slope but different endpoints is not the required graph.\n\n![The curve through the calculated points](images/82/8227fb9f808f8b7622b2d3910efa11ce6d87b8085b4d7e24a77a342306532ee4.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697897 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1bf915d8-6386-5c54-be79-20a4aeaf541b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/62/627e47bf56eb39ef2d2c76dbdc0025fe931e7dccc9a672aff34a81f10cb51ec6.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697891} {:answer/id #uuid "70f0a849-b7ae-5bf7-b634-34370e5ae990" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/02/02ee60db4d6765efaf9bde2e139017c67541afb341b144b47deb9d8e9a159e9a.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697896} {:answer/id #uuid "93455f0c-22b5-5c6e-bce7-25a8d0d6293c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/f9/f91bcece50a80cfd66cc9608a93072cd7089025b37ed09055ec7720538d037fa.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697901} {:answer/id #uuid "9591fb7f-d240-540e-b68b-21991e37a93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d369859178cc839d6f4299e44e79f80f5d8e3341a82cab4a317b8265aa75dddd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697902} {:answer/id #uuid "ae3af7bb-aeeb-504c-8499-dc8dbb741f58" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/87/87c5054212819dd11c81cb4efb4e892274d1ca290cf96547d0c287531c469f45.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697903}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9591fb7f-d240-540e-b68b-21991e37a93b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d3/d369859178cc839d6f4299e44e79f80f5d8e3341a82cab4a317b8265aa75dddd.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697902} :answer-field/id #uuid "7e6e7cbc-d38a-5510-9dc3-2ff6464a025d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697898}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7644270e-57aa-5c69-8e0b-cd91ed7f2919" :question/problem "Determine the graph of the following parametrically defined curve:\n\n$$\nx=t^2-1,\\qquad y=2-t,\\qquad -1\\leq t\\leq 2.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Create a table of paired coordinates. First calculate the $x$-values:\n\n| $t$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |\n\nNow calculate the $y$-values at the same parameter values:\n\n| $t$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $x$ | $0$ | $-1$ | $0$ | $3$ |\n| $y$ | $3$ | $2$ | $1$ | $0$ |\n\nThe points are $(0,3)$, $(-1,2)$, $(0,1)$ and $(3,0)$. As $t$ runs from $-1$ to $0$, $x$ decreases to $-1$; as $t$ runs from $0$ to $2$, $x$ increases to $3$. Meanwhile $y$ decreases throughout. Plot the smooth right-opening arc through these points. Its leftmost point is $(-1,2)$, and its included endpoints are $(0,3)$ and $(3,0)$. The two arms have different lengths because the parameter interval is asymmetric.\n\n![The curve through the calculated points](images/93/9346e80ef10f528dd956f6d11b511b106e39c9d2724a6be0c6e60f9e73afe183.png)"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697915 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "$x=-3$ requires $t=0$ or $t=-2$, both excluded. The lower bound on $x$ is strict." :answer/id #uuid "02bf8594-fd10-51bb-899f-6f0738f7db21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697909} {:answer/feedback "The lower bound on $x$ is approached at the excluded boundary, while the upper bound on $y$ is attained inside the domain." :answer/id #uuid "066c6421-e8cb-5f6b-834c-952f021293a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697910} {:answer/feedback "The vertex for $x$ is at $t=-1$, outside the allowed domain. For $t>0$, the sharper bound is $x>-3$." :answer/id #uuid "3e2acba4-386f-5964-9c3f-826c2e75ee46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -4,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697914} {:answer/feedback "The value $y=4$ occurs at the allowed parameter $t=2$; a strict parameter bound does not exclude an interior maximum." :answer/id #uuid "786dddd9-115e-5687-845d-cc23f3c97bf4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y<4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697917} {:answer/feedback "The expression $4-(t-2)^2$ is at most $4$, not at least $4$." :answer/id #uuid "e1b9c4cf-22a1-58fe-af03-812c0a4d587d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y\\ge 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697927}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The lower bound on $x$ is approached at the excluded boundary, while the upper bound on $y$ is attained inside the domain." :answer/id #uuid "066c6421-e8cb-5f6b-834c-952f021293a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y\\le 4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697910} :answer-field/id #uuid "d2d82b3f-04f3-5b41-8f57-443a382e0133" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697924}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "468940dc-fef5-52fb-97ca-09170efe4223" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2+2t-3,\\quad y=4t-t^2,\\quad t>0,\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Complete the square for each coordinate, keeping the restriction $t>0$ throughout.\n\nFor $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=t^2+2t-3 \\\\\n  &=(t+1)^2-4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe unrestricted minimum $-4$ would require $t=-1$, which is not allowed. In the given domain, $t+1>1$, so $(t+1)^2>1$ and $x>-3$. The boundary value $-3$ would require $t=0$ or $t=-2$, neither of which is allowed. Every value $x>-3$ is attained by $t=-1+\\sqrt{x+4}>0$. Thus the range of $x$ is $x>-3$.\n\nFor $y$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &=4t-t^2 \\\\\n  &=-(t-2)^2+4.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence $y\\le 4$. The maximum $4$ is attained at $t=2$, which is allowed even though the parameter inequality is strict. Every value $y\\le 4$ is attained by $t=2+\\sqrt{4-y}>0$, so there is no lower bound.\n\nTherefore, the coordinate ranges are $x>-3$ and $y\\le 4$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186697918 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/feedback "Subtracting the nonnegative quantity $t^2$ from $3$ gives an upper bound on $y$." :answer/id #uuid "160f02aa-e38a-53a2-808d-576d50bd0de1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\ge 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697911} {:answer/feedback "The minimum of $x$ is $-3$ at $t=2$, and the maximum of $y$ is $3$ at $t=0$." :answer/id #uuid "7369e6dd-083c-57ce-9a37-8a6f4f63ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697916} {:answer/feedback "The nonnegative square in $x=(t-2)^2-3$ gives a lower bound on $x$." :answer/id #uuid "cc8fccc4-9896-534b-9da8-76559ee0736c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\le -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697922} {:answer/feedback "Both extremizing parameter values are allowed, so both equalities are included." :answer/id #uuid "d71b3e40-f663-5d75-a8f1-284afa23e1a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x>-3,\\quad y<3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697925} {:answer/feedback "The constant term is not the minimum of this quadratic. Complete the square to find $(t-2)^2-3$." :answer/id #uuid "f5c05357-8df0-509d-849d-c875c630afab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge 1,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697928}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/feedback "The minimum of $x$ is $-3$ at $t=2$, and the maximum of $y$ is $3$ at $t=0$." :answer/id #uuid "7369e6dd-083c-57ce-9a37-8a6f4f63ed03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x\\ge -3,\\quad y\\le 3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697916} :answer-field/id #uuid "f5cebc80-4738-5ebe-8c01-c1b3c2fc2e72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186697929}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "921cecba-5183-5dd0-9ca3-7a72a38cdb3c" :question/problem "Given that a curve is defined parametrically as\n\n$$\nx=t^2-4t+1,\\quad y=3-t^2,\\quad t\\in(-\\infty,\\infty),\n$$\n\ndetermine the ranges of $x$ and $y$." :question/worked-solution "Consider each coordinate separately.\n\nFor $x$, complete the square:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx &=t^2-4t+1 \\\\\n  &=(t^2-4t+4)-3 \\\\\n  &=(t-2)^2-3.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe square takes every nonnegative value as $t$ ranges over all real numbers. Thus $x\\ge -3$, with equality at $t=2$, and there is no upper bound.\n\nFor $y$, the fact that $t^2\\ge 0$ gives $y=3-t^2\\le 3$. Equality occurs at $t=0$, and $y$ takes every value below $3$.\n\nTherefore, the coordinate ranges are $x\\ge -3$ and $y\\le 3$. These bounds need not occur at the same parameter value; they describe the two coordinate ranges separately."}]}
